Azul Zulu 26.32 (OpenJDK 26.0.2.1+1) licensing and source notice

Current FinGrind release tooling selects Azul Zulu 26.32.203 Community Availability builds of OpenJDK 26.0.2.1+1.
Source JDK release metadata identifies this build as IMPLEMENTOR_VERSION="Zulu26.32+203-CA" and JAVA_RUNTIME_VERSION="26.0.2.1+1".

Certain portions of Azul Zulu Builds of OpenJDK are based on OpenJDK source code and are licensed under GNU General Public License version 2 with the Classpath Exception. Azul Zulu also incorporates third-party licensed software packages. The exact selected modules' license, exception, copyright, and third-party notice files are preserved and hash-indexed under runtime/legal/ in each FinGrind bundle and container.

For portions governed by licenses that require source availability, Azul's August 2026 licensing information states that, for three years from receipt of Azul Zulu, Azul provides on request a complete machine-readable source copy on a customary software-interchange medium for no more than its physical distribution cost. The upstream source-request address used by Azul's licensing publications is azul_openJDK@azul.com.

Full Azul licensing information for this exact build:
https://docs.azul.com/core/tpls/august-2026/zulu26_jdk_tpl.html
